{
  "quest.462A91977D2113A8.title": "Magazine Subscription",
  "quest.786D4061D572DE1F.quest_desc": [
    "Tired of zombies at the front door?",
    "",
    "Place an &aInterdiction Torch&r to push mobs out of a 5-block radius around it. A few of them keep a doorway or a work area clear.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: It doesn't push arrows or fireballs. The &dBroker&r sells these torches if you'd rather keep your parts.",
  ],
  "quest.70E40C30466131CA.quest_desc": [
    "The &aPhoenix Down&r saves you from one death.",
    "",
    "Upgrade your &2Angelic Feather&r into &aPhoenix Down&r. It takes three &2Angelheart Vials&r, so check JEI for those first.",
    "",
    "When you would die, it brings you back at full health, clears bad effects and gives a short burst of resistance and regeneration, then turns back into an &2Angelic Feather&r. It keeps the feather's fall protection too.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: An &2Angelheart Vial&r on its own is the one-use version. It revives you at 25% health and then breaks.",
  ],
  "quest.462A91977D2113A8.quest_desc": [
    "A handgun is only as good as what's loaded in it.",
    "",
    "Load up a &aNeutral Magazine&r for your handgun. &2Neutral Shots&r come 8 to a craft, which is exactly one magazine's worth.",
    "",
    "Other shot types add effects, such as &2Seeker Shots&r that home in on targets. JEI lists the rest.",
  ],
  "quest.4906AA8E25E49F95.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks item duplication",
  "quest.2E430F83CE69DD48.quest_desc": [
    "Inventory full of cobblestone again? A &aVoid Tear&r holds up to two billion of a single item.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aVoid Tear&r, then Right-click it to capture whatever item you're carrying the most of. It pulls every matching stack out of your inventory straight away.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Sneak + scroll switches between taking everything, keeping one stack in your inventory and refilling your inventory from the tear.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The &2Infernal Tear&r is crafted from an unset &aVoid Tear&r, and so is the Emperor's Chalice, so you'll want more than one.",
  ],
  "quest.4906AA8E25E49F95.quest_desc": [
    "The &aTome of Alkahestry&r turns redstone into copies of your items.",
    "",
    "Craft the &aTome of Alkahestry&r and Sneak + Right-click to activate it. While it's active it absorbs redstone and glowstone from your inventory as charge, up to 1,000. A block of redstone is worth 9.",
    "",
    "Craft the tome together with an item to get extra copies for a charge cost. A gold ingot costs 32, a diamond 64 and a nether star 256. JEI's Alkahestry Tome Crafting page lists everything else it can copy.",
  ],
  "quest.71F0A28C67E53A01.title": "Reliquary",
  "quest.70E40C30466131CA.quest_subtitle": "A second chance",
  "quest.6B8E47B9CDF810B5.title": "Lock and Load",
  "task.342F6BD8B4703CE5.title": "Any Reliquary Mob Drop",
  "quest.70E40C30466131CA.title": "&6Phoenix Down",
  "quest.4D919D4079339210.title": "Glow Up",
  "quest.503E6943750FDCDD.quest_desc": [
    "Lava stops being a threat with the &aInfernal Chalice&r in your inventory.",
    "",
    "Craft the &aInfernal Chalice&r to become immune to lava damage. It needs an &2Emperor's Chalice&r, made from a spare Void Tear. It also needs the &2Infernal Claws&r, so check JEI for both recipes.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It holds 500,000 mB of lava of its own, and Sneak + Right-click switches between draining lava and placing it.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The protection costs a little hunger for each point of damage it blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.4906AA8E25E49F95.title": "&6Tome of Alkahestry",
  "quest.2E430F83CE69DD48.title": "&6Void Tear",
  "quest.503E6943750FDCDD.title": "&6Infernal Chalice",
  "quest.1A3041B4C0EA8796.quest_subtitle": "Banks your experience",
  "quest.3EC7D38B078C2228.title": "Charmed, I'm Sure",
  "quest.1A3041B4C0EA8796.quest_desc": [
    "All that experience from the &2Infernal Tear&r needs somewhere safe to go.",
    "",
    "Craft the &aHero's Medallion&r to bank your levels. It fills from your levels until you drop to the level you set with Sneak + scroll, and Right-click gives levels back.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Put it in a &2Pedestal&r and it repairs Mending items in other pedestals within 5 blocks, spending 5 experience per repair step. Leave your tools there between trips.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: A pedestal only works while it's switched on. Right-click its switch with an empty hand or give it a redstone signal.",
  ],
  "quest.2631D88BB09AE9C8.title": "Storm Chaser",
  "quest.2631D88BB09AE9C8.quest_desc": [
    "Charged creepers are the only mobs that drop the &aEye of the Storm&r, and only when you kill them yourself.",
    "",
    "Hunt for an &aEye of the Storm&r during a thunderstorm. Lightning charges creepers, and a trident with &2Channeling&r lets you call it down yourself.",
    "",
    "&2Storm Shots&r from the handgun charge creepers too.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The &2Tome of Alkahestry&r needs one, so hold on to it.",
  ],
  "quest.77462803DD585713.title": "Light as a Feather",
  "quest.77462803DD585713.quest_desc": [
    "A long fall is the quickest way to die far from home.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aAngelic Feather&r and keep it in your inventory. Fall damage stops, and you get a small jump boost as well.",
    "",
    "Each fall it saves you from costs hunger instead, so carry food if you plan to rely on it for long drops.",
  ],
  "quest.3EC7D38B078C2228.quest_desc": [
    "Each &2Mob Charm&r makes one mob type ignore you. A charm starts with 80 durability, loses 1 for every mob of its type you kill, and each of that mob's special drops repairs 20.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aCharm Belt&r to wear every charm you have in one belt slot.",
    "",
    "A charm or the &aCharm Belt&r placed in a &2Pedestal&r keeps those mobs from attacking players within 21 blocks.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Fragments for mobs without a part recipe drop directly, at roughly 1 in 60 kills.",
  ],
  "quest.503E6943750FDCDD.quest_subtitle": "Lava protection",
  "quest.786D4061D572DE1F.title": "Keep Out",
  "quest.6BD39D9678CDEF82.quest_desc": [
    "Mob drops scatter everywhere, and the &aCoin of Fortune&r brings them to you.",
    "",
    "Craft a &aCoin of Fortune&r and Sneak + Right-click to turn it on. It pulls items and experience toward you from 5 blocks away.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Hold Right-click for a stronger pull that reaches 15 blocks, useful for sweeping up the floor of a mob farm.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: In a &2Pedestal&r, an active coin puts what it collects into containers next to the pedestal.",
  ],
  "quest.57784C221BB8C84C.title": "Up in Smoke",
  "quest.2E430F83CE69DD48.quest_subtitle": "Unlocks the Infernal Tear",
  "quest.4D919D4079339210.quest_desc": [
    "Glowstone charges the tome as well as redstone does, and the &aAltar of Light&r grows it for you.",
    "",
    "Place the &aAltar of Light&r in direct sunlight and Right-click it with redstone until it activates, which takes 3.",
    "",
    "About 20 to 25 minutes later a glowstone block appears on top. Right-click the altar with the &2Tome of Alkahestry&r to fuel it from the tome's charge instead of your own redstone.",
  ],
  "quest.6BD39D9678CDEF82.title": "Pocket Change",
  "quest.1A3041B4C0EA8796.title": "&6Hero's Medallion",
  "quest.57784C221BB8C84C.quest_desc": [
    "Your &2Void Tear&r stores junk. The &aInfernal Tear&r burns it into experience instead.",
    "",
    "Craft an &aInfernal Tear&r and Right-click it to set it to the burnable item you carry the most of. Then Sneak + Right-click to turn on auto-absorb.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Values run from 1 experience for netherrack or gravel to 4 for gunpowder and 32 for a diamond. Gunpowder from a creeper farm is a good steady supply.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: Auto-absorb starts switched off, so nothing burns until you turn it on.",
  ],
  "quest.71F0A28C67E53A01.quest_desc": [
    "&eReliquary&r builds its relics from rare parts that monsters drop only when you kill them yourself.",
    "",
    "Bring back any &aReliquary mob drop&r to get started. A zombie, for example, drops a &2Zombie Heart&r. Each part's tooltip names the mob it comes from.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Every kill rolls twice at 2%. &bLooting&r improves one roll and &bSevering&r improves the other, up to 52% at Severing V. Severing comes from the enchanting table on melee weapons.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The parts have no crafting recipe in this pack. A few turn up in dungeon, temple and stronghold chests, but a mob farm that kills without you gets nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.6B8E47B9CDF810B5.quest_desc": [
    "Some fights are better started from a distance.",
    "",
    "Build the &aHunter's Handgun&r. Right-click fires, and holding Right-click reloads from a magazine in your inventory.",
    "",
    "Your experience level sets how fast it reloads and how short the delay between shots is, and it's at its best from level 20.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: The &dSwashbuckler&r sells the gun and Neutral Magazines if you'd rather buy than build.",
  ],
}